      "message": "nit. Since it looks like you are using the C API directly, I\u0027d suggest using the INIT macros we provide for this initialization (here and in other relevant places below). It also allows you to omit setting the `sType` manually which can be error-prone. The macros look something like `WGPU_SHARED_TEXTURE_MEMORY_A_HARDWARE_BUFFER_DESCRIPTOR_INIT`.\n\nAlternatively, would it be possible to use the C++ API instead of the C API? I think it would be a lot easier for handling all the manual reference counting you are doing which can often be a source of memory leaks that are hard to catch. Plus it actually looks like you are using some C++ APIs (for enums and stuff, i.e. any of the `wgpu::*` stuff) already, so maybe it would be best to limit the C API to only places where we absolutely need it?",
